'' A BYDESC PARAMETER OF A BUILTIN ELEMENT DOES NOT TAKE A UDT ARRAY, NOR THE OTHER WAY
'' ROUND (T83). The element check compared two UDTs or two builtins and never one of each,
'' so a Decimal array went to DecimalApportion's 'weights( ) as longint', which read each
'' 16-byte element as an 8-byte integer: 100.00 in three came out 0.00, 100.00, 0.00. See
'' src/symbols/arrayelem.bas.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 with -maxerr inf over the source, 2026-10-03: error 58 on lines
'' 20-23 and 99 on 24, and no others --
''
''     20-21  a UDT array, of 16 and of 8 bytes, to 'a( ) as longint'
''     22-23  a longint and a string array to 'a( ) as D'
''     24     a UDT array to an overload SET: TKO0632 alone, not a second report
''     25-28  the matching arrays, accepted
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/bydesc-udt-builtin.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: bydesc-udt-builtin.bas(20,5): error TKO0687: a bydesc parameter takes an array of exactly its element type
'' EXPECT-OUT: bydesc-udt-builtin.bas(21,6): error TKO0687
'' EXPECT-OUT: bydesc-udt-builtin.bas(22,5): error TKO0687
'' EXPECT-OUT: bydesc-udt-builtin.bas(23,5): error TKO0687
'' EXPECT-OUT: bydesc-udt-builtin.bas(24,2): error TKO0632
'' EXPECT-NOT: (24,5)
'' EXPECT-NOT: (25,
'' EXPECT-NOT: (26,
'' EXPECT-NOT: (27,
'' EXPECT-NOT: (28,
